01:03:38,571 --> 01:03:44,571
Black Panther: Wakanda Forever is a 2022 American superhero film based on
Marvel Comics featuring the character Shuri / Black Panther.

12
01:09:25,714 --> 01:09:31,714
Produced by Marvel Studios and distributed by Walt Disney Studios Motion Pictures, it is the sequel
to Black Panther (2018) and the 30th film in the Marvel Cinematic Universe (MCU).

13
01:15:12,857 --> 01:15:18,857
Directed by Ryan Coogler, who co-wrote the screenplay with Joe Robert Cole, the film stars Letitia Wright as Shuri / Black Panther, alongside Lupita Nyong'o, Danai Gurira,
Winston Duke, Florence Kasumba, Dominique Thorne, Michaela Coel, Mabel Cadena, Tenoch Huerta Mejía, Martin Freeman, Julia Louis-Dreyfus, and Angela Bassett.

14
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:06,000
In the film, the leaders of Wakanda fight to protect their
nation in the wake of King T'Challa's death.

15
01:26:47,142 --> 01:26:53,142
Ideas for a sequel began after the release of Black Panther in February 2018.

16
01:32:34,285 --> 01:32:40,285
Coogler negotiated to return as director in the following months, and Marvel
Studios officially confirmed the sequel's development in mid-2019.

17
01:38:21,428 --> 01:38:27,428
Plans for the film changed in August 2020 when Black Panther star and T'Challa actor Chadwick
Boseman died from colon cancer, with Marvel choosing not to recast his role.

18
01:44:08,571 --> 01:44:14,571
The return of other main cast members from the first film was confirmed that November, and the
sequel's title was revealed to be Black Panther: Wakanda Forever in May 2021.

19
01:49:55,714 --> 01:50:01,714
Filming began in late June in Atlanta, taking place at both Trilith Studios and Tyler Perry Studios, before moving to
Massachusetts in August, but was halted in November to allow Wright to recover from an injury sustained during filming.

20
01:55:42,857 --> 01:55:48,857
It resumed by mid-January 2022 and wrapped in late March in Puerto Rico.

21
02:01:30,000 --> 02:01:36,000
Black Panther: Wakanda Forever premiered at the El Capitan Theatre and the Dolby Theatre in Hollywood, Los Angeles, on October
26, 2022, and was released in the United States on November 11, as the final film in Phase Four of the MCU.

22
02:07:17,142 --> 02:07:23,142
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and grossed $859.2
million worldwide, becoming the sixth-highest-grossing film of 2022.

23
02:13:04,285 --> 02:13:10,285
Wakanda Forever and Bassett's performance received numerous awards and nominations, including five Academy Awards (winning Costume Design), one British
Academy Film Award, six Critics' Choice Movie Awards (winning two), two Golden Globe Awards (winning one), and two Screen Actors Guild Awards.

24
02:18:51,428 --> 02:18:57,428
A spin-off miniseries focusing on Thorne's Riri
Williams, Ironheart, premiered in June 2025.

25
02:24:38,571 --> 02:24:44,571
A sequel is in development for an expected 2028 release.

26
02:30:25,714 --> 02:30:31,714
The film explores themes of hero, loss of loved one,
superhero, royal family, based on comic.

27
02:36:12,857 --> 02:36:18,857
The tone is thought_provoking.
